{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile + transformer (config_006) is our best result at 0.653 acc, while image-only resnet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208 acc. The critical open question is whether multimodal fusion adds value or merely injects noise from the weak image branch. Config_032 takes our best-validated RNA pipeline (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) and adds the simplest image component (resnet50, concat fusion), directly testing whether complementary image signal improves over the RNA-only ceiling. If accuracy exceeds ~0.653, multimodal is a promising direction and we can then optimize the image encoder (ViT-L) and fusion strategy. If it drops below 0.653, it indicates resnet50 image features are net noise, prompting a test of ViT-L before further multimodal investment. This is the highest-information single experiment because it resolves the largest remaining uncertainty—whether the image modality is worth pursuing at all—while exploiting our strongest RNA evidence rather than re-testing lower-priority questions like aggregation for PCA or scgpt in multiprofile."
}

